# LexicRo scheduled jobs -- the single source of truth for this host's crontab.
#
# Install:  sudo crontab /opt/lexicro/scripts/crontab
# Verify:   sudo crontab -l
#
# NOTE: `crontab <file>` REPLACES root's entire crontab. As of 2026-08-26 these
# three jobs are the only entries; check `sudo crontab -l` before installing in
# case something else has been added by hand since.
#
# No line carries a secret. Each script reads its own ping URL from
# /opt/lexicro/.env -- BACKUP_HEALTHCHECK_URL and API_HEALTHCHECK_URL -- so this
# file is safe to paste into an issue or a runbook. That was not always true --
# the ping URL used to sit inline on the backup line and leaked twice by being
# copied around.
#
# The two healthchecks.io checks watch different things and neither speaks for
# the other: the backup check stays green through a total API outage, and the
# API check stays green through a failed backup. Until 2026-08-26 only the first
# existed, named "LexicRo Health" and tagged `api database health service`,
# which invited exactly the wrong reading of a green tick.
#
# cron runs with a minimal PATH: docker is called by absolute path below, and
# both shell scripts set their own PATH for the same reason.

# Database dump, verification, and request_log retention. 03:17 -- an odd minute
# so it does not collide with everything else on the host firing at exactly 03:00.
17 3 * * * /bin/bash /opt/lexicro/scripts/backup.sh >> /var/log/lexicro-backup.log 2>&1

# Purge expired, unconsumed key requests. Deliberately after the backup, so each
# night's dump captures the pre-purge state.
0 4 * * * cd /opt/lexicro && /usr/bin/docker compose exec -T api python scripts/purge_key_requests.py >> /var/log/lexicro-purge.log 2>&1

# Probe the public API and ping its own check. Every 10 minutes: frequent enough
# that an outage is noticed quickly, infrequent enough to stay invisible in the
# access log. How fast it actually alerts is set by the check's grace period on
# healthchecks.io, not by this interval -- set the grace to ~25 min so a single
# missed run does not page, but two in a row do.
*/10 * * * * /bin/bash /opt/lexicro/scripts/probe_api.sh >> /var/log/lexicro-probe.log 2>&1
